From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Dalessio <mike.dalessio@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 13:26:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(CRuby): use-after-free in Document#encoding= when
 setter raises

When Document#encoding= received input that made StringValueCStr
raise (e.g. a string containing a null byte), the document's current
encoding string had already been freed before the raise, leaving
doc->encoding pointing at freed memory. A subsequent call to
Document#encoding would then read invalid memory.

Evaluate and duplicate the new encoding before freeing the old one, so
the document is left in a consistent state if StringValueCStr raises.

ref: https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-5v8h-3h3q-446p

Fixes: CVE-2026-57236

[Shivani: backported to nokogiri-1.13.6; dropped the JRuby-only
XmlDocument.java hunk since this package ships only the CRuby C
extension]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
 ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c b/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
index 1af62ac..44adef4 100644
--- a/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
+++ b/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
@@ -210,13 +210,16 @@ static VALUE
 set_encoding(VALUE self, VALUE encoding)
 {
   xmlDocPtr doc;
+  xmlChar *new_encoding;
   Data_Get_Struct(self, xmlDoc, doc);
 
+  new_encoding = xmlStrdup((xmlChar *)StringValueCStr(encoding));
+
   if (doc->encoding) {
     xmlFree(DISCARD_CONST_QUAL_XMLCHAR(doc->encoding));
   }
 
-  doc->encoding = xmlStrdup((xmlChar *)StringValueCStr(encoding));
+  doc->encoding = new_encoding;
 
   return encoding;
 }
